The input you provided is already in a structured JSON format. However, if you want to convert it into the specified output format, you can use a JSON parser to parse the input and then format it as required. Here's an example using Python:

```python
import json

input_str = "{"output_list": [{"function_name": "transfer","code": "function transfer(address _to, uint256 _value) {             _transfer(msg.sender, _to, _value);         }","vulnerability": "Token Transfer","reason": "The transfer function does not check if the sender has enough tokens to send. It directly sends the tokens to the recipient."}]}"

output = json.loads(input_str)

formatted_output = {
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": output["output_list"][0]["function_name"],
            "code": output["output_list"][0]["code"],
            "vulnerability": output["output_list"][0]["vulnerability"],
            "reason": output["output_list"][0]["reason"]
        }
    ]
}

print(json.dumps(formatted_output, indent=4))
```

This will output the following JSON:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "transfer",
            "code": "function transfer(address _to, uint256 _value) {             _transfer(msg.sender, _to, _value);         }",
            "vulnerability": "Token Transfer",
            "reason": "The transfer function does not check if the sender has enough tokens to send. It directly sends the tokens to the recipient."
        }
    ]
}
```

Note that the input JSON is already in the desired format, so there's no need to make any changes. However, if you want to parse a different input and format it as specified, you can replace the `input_str` variable with your input.